From 92c9adb93ed201e4edff49b8462c6e6b73375cc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 01:05:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] P5-printing-module-printer-registry-service

Printing Module, Phase 5 (Printer registry service + controller, full CRUD, decision Q-01/Q-09):

- PrinterConfigurationService: GetAll/GetById open to tenant (scoped) and admin; Create/Update/
  SoftDelete/Restore all gated to system admin via PrintingErrors.PrinterOnlySystemAdmin.
  ValidateMaticaPayloadShape shared by Create/Update so the Matica-required/Evolis-rejected rule
  can't drift between them. Soft-delete/restore cascade to the Matica extension row (same
  aggregate reasoning as the product print-config module).
- PrintersController: full CRUD, one-liner bodies, matches BranchController's exact route/verb
  conventions (DELETE = soft delete, POST {id}/restore).
- IServiceManager / ServiceManager: IPrinterConfigurationService wired through (13/13 property
  parity verified by script).
- InfrastructureServiceRegistration: IPrinterConfigurationService + its Func<> registered.

Domain/Infrastructure corrections needed to make P1's Printer/MaticaPrinterConfiguration
entities actually usable from a service (metadata only - no new columns, no migration beyond
what P1 already produced):
- Printer.Branch and MaticaPrinterConfiguration.Printer navigation properties added. Without
  the latter, creating a printer and its Matica configuration in one transaction was not
  actually possible: MaticaPrinterConfiguration.PrinterId can't be set until the printer's
  identity is generated by SaveChanges, and IUnitOfWork.ExecuteInTransactionAsync's contract
  forbids the work delegate from calling SaveChanges itself to get that id early. The
  navigation lets EF Core's change tracker fix up the FK automatically within the one
  SaveChanges call instead (same mechanism BranchRequest/BranchRequestItem already rely on).
- AppDbContext.ConfigurePrinterRegistry updated to configure both relationships through the
  navigations instead of HasOne<T>() with no navigation.
- PrinterRepo.GetPagedAsync / GetByIdIncludingDeletedAsync now .Include(p => p.Branch), so
  PrinterResponse.BranchName (defined back in P2) is actually populated instead of always empty.

Bug caught during review before commit: MaticaPrinterConfigurations.PrinterId is uniquely
constrained unconditionally (no soft-delete filter on the index), but GetByPrinterIdAsync
respects the standard IsDeleted query filter. Combined, RestoreAsync could never find a
soft-deleted Matica config to restore it (silently stuck deleted forever), and UpdateAsync's
self-heal path could try to insert a duplicate PrinterId and hit the unique constraint. Added
IMaticaPrinterConfigRepo.GetByPrinterIdIncludingDeletedAsync and used it in both RestoreAsync
and UpdateAsync's self-heal branch; UpdateAsync now also un-deletes a found-but-deleted row
instead of only handling the missing-row case.
